Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  Report Status  Signed  Type  Surgical Pathology  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  DIAGNOSIS   A  Left breast  excisional biopsy   Low grade phyllodes tumor 4 0cm   See note    Fibrocystic changes   Small intraductal papilloma   B  Left breast  excisional biopsy   Fibrocystic changes  adenosis and ductal hyperplasia  see note   Fibroadenoma 0 7cm  with ductal hyperplasia   NOTE  In specimen A  the phyllodes tumor is present at the inked specimen  edges  The entire case was sent to Massachusetts General Hospital to  Dr  Melinda Fan Lerwill who concurs with our diagnosis  She adds    I would classify the mass in part A as a low grade phyllodes tumor   The primary features that help to distinguish it from a fibroadenoma are  its morphologic heterogeneity and the presence of irregular  leaf like  fronds  The morphologic heterogeneity is manifest in several ways   There is variation in the stromal cellularity  from regions that are  essentially acellular and hyalinized to regions that are moderately  hypercellular  There is variation in the distribution of glands to  stroma  with some areas demonstrating more pronounced expansion of the  stromal compartment  The glands are also heterogeneous with irregular  dilated contours  All these features contrast with the uniform  cellularity  consistent distribution of glands to stroma  and regular  intracanalicular or pericanalicular glands typically seen in  fibroadenomas  I also found up to 4 stromal mitotic figures per 10 high  power fields in one of the more cellular regions of the tumor  which  would be a higher rate that expected for a fibroadenoma  There are a  few areas where there do appear to be genuine fronds projecting into  dilated ducts and or cystic spaces  a features that I consider a very  strong indicator of the diagnosis of phyllodes tumor  Stromal  overgrowth is absent  and the tumor extends to the margins of the  excision  At our institution  we generally do not make a diagnosis of  benign phyllodes tumor  since even tumors with  benign  histologic  features can recur and in extremely rare instances metastasize  We  prefer instead a low  intermediate and high grade classification scheme  for these neoplasms   The epithelial proliferations in slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  appear to be usual   type ductal hyperplasia  The cells are overlapping  show maturation   have nuclear grooves and lack polarization  all features that support an  interpretation of usual type rather than atypical ductal hyperplasia   Similarly  I would also characterize the epithelial proliferation in  part B as florid usual type ductal hyperplasia  Although the cells are  little larger in slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   they are still overlapping  have nuclear  grooves  and lack polarization  They do not demonstrate the monotonous  hyperchromatic morphology of cells typically seen in low grade atypia    Final Diagnosis by  Nicole A  Mihok  M D   Clinical diagnosis   history   Left breast mass  Tissue Designation   A Breast  excision with margins   left  B Breast  excision with margins   left  Gross description   The specimen is received in formalin in two containers   Specimen A labeled  left index fibroadenoma   designated  breast  on the jar  and consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE gram  bosselated  oval shaped  white tissue  that is up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  It is not oriented  The margins are inked  black  The cut section shows rubbery  white parenchyma with a slightly bulging  cut surface that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The entire specimen is submitted  in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   18 agg  all   Specimen B labeled  left breast    fibroadenoma  consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE  gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  portion of tissue received in formalin  It is not  oriented  The margins are inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and  shows a variegated  tan yellow portion of tissue  The entire specimen is  submitted from one end towards the other in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   6 agg  all   Dictated by  NAM____ signature on file ____RICHARD SAMPSON  M D  REMOVED_DATE  Final   ____ signature on file ____NICOLE MIHOK  M D  REMOVED_DATE  Final    report_end  , no_CancerNOS.
